/S /H1
/T (Microwave imaging has emerged as a powerful non-invasive diagnostic tool in biomedical  engineering. It leverages electromagnetic waves to reconstruct internal structures, enabling  clinicians to identify and characterize abnormalities. One of its most promising applications  lies in breast cancer detection, offering a low-risk alternative to traditional imaging techniques. )
/E (Microwave imaging has emerged as a powerful non-invasive diagnostic tool in biomedical  engineering. It leverages electromagnetic waves to reconstruct internal structures, enabling  clinicians to identify and characterize abnormalities. One of its most promising applications  lies in breast cancer detection, offering a low-risk alternative to traditional imaging techniques. )
/Pg 13 0 R
