/T (In the context of biomedical imaging, ISPs are used to reconstruct the dielectric properties of tissues, which vary between healthy and abnormal regions. For example, cancerous tissues have higher permittivity and conductivity compared to normal tissues. This contrast forms the basis for tumor detection using microwave imaging. By solving the ISP, clinicians can obtain high-resolution maps of the internal tissue structure, aiding in early diagnosis.  6. Traditional Approaches to Solving ISPs  Several conventional algorithms have been developed to address ISPs, each with its strengths and limitations: )
