<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The Born Iterative Method \(BIM\) is a widely adopted technique for solving inverse scattering problems \(ISP\), particularly in the context of electromagnetic wave interactions with heterogeneous media. By iteratively refining the solution, BIM addresses the complexities of reconstructing the dielectric properties of a medium. Its iterative nature and relatively straightforward implementation have made BIM a cornerstone for applications like biomedical imaging, geophysics, and nondestructive testing. )
/E (The Born Iterative Method \(BIM\) is a widely adopted technique for solving inverse scattering problems \(ISP\), particularly in the context of electromagnetic wave interactions with heterogeneous media. By iteratively refining the solution, BIM addresses the complexities of reconstructing the dielectric properties of a medium. Its iterative nature and relatively straightforward implementation have made BIM a cornerstone for applications like biomedical imaging, geophysics, and nondestructive testing. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
