458 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The BIM relies on the Born approximation, which simplifies the scattering problem by assuming that the scattered field is linearly proportional to the contrast between the scatterer and the surrounding medium. While this assumption holds for weak scatterers where the contrast is small, it becomes less accurate for strong scatterers, such as dense tumors in breast imaging. This limitation necessitates iterative refinements to account for the nonlinearities introduced by stronger scatterers. )
/E (The BIM relies on the Born approximation, which simplifies the scattering problem by assuming that the scattered field is linearly proportional to the contrast between the scatterer and the surrounding medium. While this assumption holds for weak scatterers where the contrast is small, it becomes less accurate for strong scatterers, such as dense tumors in breast imaging. This limitation necessitates iterative refinements to account for the nonlinearities introduced by stronger scatterers. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
