/E (assumes weak scattering. In cases involving strong scatterers, such as dense tumors, the method may fail to converge or produce inaccurate results. Computational Intensity: Each iteration requires solving the forward problem, leading to high computational costs, especially for large datasets or high-resolution reconstructions. Dependence on Initial Estimates: The accuracy of the reconstruction is heavily influenced by the quality of the initial guess, making it challenging to achieve reliable results in complex scenarios. )
