518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The Born Iterative Method remains a cornerstone of inverse scattering problems, providing a robust framework for reconstructing complex media. While its limitations in handling strong scatterers and computational intensity are well-known, advancements such as quadratic programming and machine learning integration are addressing these challenges. In biomedical imaging, particularly breast cancer detection, BIM continues to play a pivotal role, offering a pathway to accurate, non-invasive diagnostics. )
/E (The Born Iterative Method remains a cornerstone of inverse scattering problems, providing a robust framework for reconstructing complex media. While its limitations in handling strong scatterers and computational intensity are well-known, advancements such as quadratic programming and machine learning integration are addressing these challenges. In biomedical imaging, particularly breast cancer detection, BIM continues to play a pivotal role, offering a pathway to accurate, non-invasive diagnostics. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
